   7:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h **** namespace daisy
   8:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h **** {
   9:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h **** /** @brief Hardare timer peripheral support.
  10:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** 
  11:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** Supports general-function TIM peripherals:
  12:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** - TIM2, TIM3, TIM4, TIM5
  13:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  **
  14:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** DaisySeed, and many internal peripherals utilize TIM2 for timing/delay purposes.
  15:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** It is configured to be at the maximum frequency: typically 200MHz or 240MHz (boost) 
  16:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** for measuring/delaying for very short periods. 
  17:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  **
  18:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** The GetUs/GetMs functions are available for convenience (and backwards compatibility),
  19:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** but to avoid wrapping errors on math when doing time-delta calculations, using ticks is 
  20:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** recommended. The data can be converted to the final time-base after getting the difference in t
  21:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** (Using GetFreq() can be used for these time-base calculations).
  22:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  **
  23:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** User callbacks can be set, and changed at any point during operation. However,
  24:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** the Config::enable_irq must be set to true when initializing for the interrupts
  25:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** to turn on and function.
  26:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  **
  27:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** @todo Fix issues with realtime getters, and wrapping of the timer(s).
  28:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  **     - This very noticeable with default settings for the 16-bit counters.
  29:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** @todo Other General purpose timers
ARM GAS  C:\Users\matth\AppData\Local\Temp\ccC5cHNR.s 			page 2


  30:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** @todo Non-internal clock sources
  31:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  ** @todo Use of the four-tim channels per tim
  32:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  **     - PWM, etc.
  33:../../../DaisyExamples/libDaisy//src/per/tim.h ****  **     - InputCapture/OutputCompare, etc.
